    "notes": "Hindi is an Indo-Aryan language that grew out of Sauraseni Prakrit, from the Old Indo-Aryan family that includes Sanskrit. Spoken Hindi and Urdu share a base (Hindustani) and are largely mutually intelligible; Urdu is written in the Arabic script and draws more on Arabic and Persian words. The other languages listed are Indo-Aryan cousins, not mutually intelligible with Hindi. Broad family metadata for orientation only; this record describes Standard Hindi."
